            "content": [
              {
                "text": "**Analyzing Grid Transformation**\n\nI'm currently dissecting Example 1 of the grid transformation task. I've noted the input frame, its dimensions, and how elements are positioned within it. My focus is on understanding the spatial relationships and how these elements relate to the larger grid transformation objective. I'm moving toward identifying a pattern or rule based on these positions.\n\n\n**Deciphering Spatial Relationships**\n\nI've zeroed in on the transformations of the frame's corner elements. Observing that (1,1) becomes 4, (1,7) becomes 3, (7,1) becomes 2, and (7,7) becomes 1 helps in understanding the pattern. I verified the outer corner coordinate correspondence. Now, I'm examining the inside-frame elements. The rotation seems to be inverted/rotated 180 degrees through the box's center. It looks like the values from inside are put outside in this way.\n\n\n",
                "type": "reasoning_text"
              }
            ],
