              {
                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following rule:\n\n1. Locate the rectangular frame of a uniform color and identify the background color.\n2. Inside the frame, there are 4 colored pixels located at the 4 inner corners:\n   - top-left\n   - top-right\n   - bottom-left\n   - bottom-right\n3. Clear the inside of the frame to the background color.\n4. Move each of the 4 corner pixels diagonally across the center to the position 1 step diagonally outside the frame's outer corners (a 180\u00b0 inversion):\n   - The inner bottom-right pixel moves to 1 step diagonally beyond the top-left outer corner `(r_min - 1, c_min - 1)`.\n   - The inner bottom-left pixel moves to 1 step diagonally beyond the top-right outer corner `(r_min - 1, c_max + 1)`.\n   - The inner top-right pixel moves to 1 step diagonally beyond the bottom-left outer corner `(r_max + 1, c_min - 1)`.\n   - The inner top-left pixel moves to 1 step diagonally beyond the bottom-right outer corner `(r_max + 1, c_max + 1)`.\n\nPlease provide the test input grid!",
